				"A group of four blue-and-yellow macaws and one green parrot huddle together on a metal platform under a thatched roof. Two hands enter the frame from the left and right, moving to grasp the birds. As the hands make contact, the entire group of parrots instantly transforms into a single, cohesive piece of soft, malleable clay. The vibrant blue, yellow, and green colors of the parrots' feathers are preserved on the surface of the new clay-like object. The hands then proceed to squish and knead the mass, with thumbs pressing deep into the center, deforming its shape in a satisfying, soft-body interaction. Throughout the entire sequence, the camera remains perfectly static, and the blurry background with green foliage and wooden structures is completely unchanged."
